uck or move to an actionable folder. If you (or someone else) still need to do something, keep it where you can find it.\n- Reference or proof: tuck away. Legal, tax, receipts, contracts, or anything you might need to prove something later.\n- Ongoing projects: tuck away. Keep only current project threads; archive or label completed project threads.\n- Sentimental but rare: tuck selectively. Keep only a few things that actually matter — don’t save every “nice” message.\n- Duplicate or copied elsewhere: delete. If the content is saved in a document or system you control, remove the email.\n- Long‑term searchable value: tuck. If it’s hard to recreate and you might search for it (credentials, setup steps, vendor details), archive it.\n- Newsletter/subscription you ignore: delete or unsubscribe. If you never open it, delete — better yet, unsubscribe.\n\nQuick habit: when you open an email, decide in 5–10 seconds: delete, act, or file. If you can’t decide, create a short “decide later” folder and empty it weekly.","runId":"run_0129a7e9a2e6730b","sampleIndex":1,"schemaVersion":"2.0.0","status":"completed","strategy":"full_policy","structuralRetention":{"allArtifactCriticalPoliciesRetained":true,"criticalPolicyIds":["universal_honesty","no_hidden_reasoning_reveal","no_background_work_claims","do_not_mention_internal_policy","do_not_invent_facts","no_raw_tool_json_exposure","privacy_floor","current_info_requires_web","asynchronous_work_request","external_email_forward_confirmation","external_state_change_confirmation","no_current_facts_from_memory","destructive_email_calendar_confirm","image_generation_requires_tool","policy_bypass_refusal","recurring_calendar_cancellation_scope","send_email_requires_explicit_request","authoritative_sources_preferred","calendar_event_mutation_policies","email_calendar_privacy","preserve_legal_effect_in_rewrites","unknown_person_no_identification","sensitive_attributes_no_inference","image_interpretation_requires_inspection","preserve_spread